int total = 0;
for (int k = 5; k > 0; k--) {
    total += k;
}
System.out.println(total);
```', '{"A":"10","B":"0","C":"15","D":"5"}', 'C', NULL, 'k = 5,4,3,2,1; total = 5+4+3+2+1 = `15`. The decrementing `for` is equivalent to a `while` with `k--` at the bottom.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q26', 'ap_csa', '2.9', '2', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
```java
int n = 4729, sum = 0;
while (n > 0) {
    sum += n % 10;
    n = n / 10;
}
System.out.println(sum);
```', '{"A":"22","B":"4729","C":"9","D":"18"}', 'A', NULL, 'Peels off last digits: 9, 2, 7, 4 → sum = 9+2+7+4 = `22`.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q27', 'ap_csa', '2.9', '2', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
```java
int count = 0;
for (int i = 1; i <= 30; i++) {
    if (i % 4 == 0) count++;
}
System.out.println(count);
```', '{"A":"6","B":"8","C":"4","D":"7"}', 'D', NULL, 'Multiples of 4 in 1..30: 4,8,12,16,20,24,28 → `7`.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q28', 'ap_csa', '2.9', '2', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
```java
int[] data = {3, 9, 2, 9, 7};
int max = data[0];
for (int i = 1; i < data.length; i++) {
    if (data[i] > max) max = data[i];
}
System.out.println(max);
```', '{"A":"7","B":"9","C":"3","D":"2"}', 'B', NULL, 'Standard max scan: starts at 3, updates to 9, stays 9 (the `>` keeps the first 9; either 9 gives the same value). Max = `9`.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q29', 'ap_csa', '1.15', '1', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
```java
String s = "programming";
System.out.println(s.substring(3, 7));
```', '{"A":"ogra","B":"ramm","C":"gram","D":"gramm"}', 'C', NULL, 'Indices 3,4,5,6 (the `to` index 7 is **excluded**). `p(0)r(1)o(2)g(3)r(4)a(5)m(6)` → `gram` (length = 7−3 = 4).', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q30', 'ap_csa', '1.15', '1', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
```java
String s = "abcdef";
System.out.println(s.substring(4));
```', '{"A":"def","B":"ef","C":"cdef","D":"e"}', 'B', NULL, '`substring(4)` returns from index 4 to the end: characters at 4 (`e`) and 5 (`f`) → `ef`.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q31', 'ap_csa', '1.15', '1', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
```java
String s = "banana";
System.out.println(s.indexOf("na"));
```', '{"A":"1","B":"2","C":"4","D":"-1"}', 'B', NULL, '`indexOf` returns the **first** occurrence: `b(0)a(1)n(2)a(3)...`, "na" first starts at index 2.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q32', 'ap_csa', '2.10', '2', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
```java
String s = "hello";
String out = "";
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
    out = s.substring(i, i + 1) + out;
}
System.out.println(out);
```', '{"A":"hello","B":"o","C":"h","D":"olleh"}', 'D', NULL, 'Each char (`s.substring(i, i+1)`) is prepended, reversing the string: `olleh`. (This is the in-syllabus reverse algorithm; there is no `charAt`.)', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q33', 'ap_csa', '2.10', '2', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is the result?
```java
String s = "abc";
System.out.println(s.substring(2, 4));
```', '{"A":"c","B":"bc","C":"An empty string","D":"A `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException` is thrown."}', 'D', NULL, '`s` has length 3 (valid indices 0..2). `substring(2, 4)` needs index up to 3, which is out of range → `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException`.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q34', 'ap_csa', '2.10', '2', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
```java
String csv = "red,green,blue,yellow";
String[] parts = csv.split(",");
System.out.println(parts.length + " " + parts[2]);
```', '{"A":"4 blue","B":"3 blue","C":"4 green","D":"4 yellow"}', 'A', NULL, '`split(",")` on a literal comma gives `["red","green","blue","yellow"]` — length 4; index 2 is `blue`.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-ac-q35', 'ap_csa', '2.11', '2', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What is printed?
